WEBVTT

00:00:28.561 --> 00:00:29.858
Ouch.

00:00:29.929 --> 00:00:31.191
Wake up.

00:00:31.264 --> 00:00:32.856
Who's there?

00:00:32.932 --> 00:00:34.524
Naomi.

00:00:34.601 --> 00:00:36.865
Come back later.

00:00:36.936 --> 00:00:38.335
You know what I think?

00:00:38.405 --> 00:00:40.896
I think you're scared
of the tree monster.

00:00:51.284 --> 00:00:55.880
I'm not scared of any tree
monster, Miss Wildman,

00:00:55.955 --> 00:01:00.016
but, as you know,
I need my beauty sleep.

00:01:00.093 --> 00:01:02.721
I'm sorry I woke you,
but we have a mission.

00:01:02.796 --> 00:01:04.661
You and your missions.

00:01:04.731 --> 00:01:07.529
Lucky for you,
your old pal Flotter

00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:09.158
has everything ready.

00:01:09.235 --> 00:01:10.361
Follow me.

00:01:12.705 --> 00:01:14.502
I've laid a trap.

00:01:14.574 --> 00:01:17.168
When he climbs this tree,
he'll trip the alarm.

00:01:18.678 --> 00:01:21.772
Tree monsters are terrified
of high-pitched noises.

00:01:21.848 --> 00:01:23.008
I never heard that.

00:01:23.083 --> 00:01:24.675
Ah! It's a well-known fact.

00:01:24.751 --> 00:01:27.686
The bell will scare him
high into those branches

00:01:27.754 --> 00:01:30.279
where counterweights
will bend the treetop

00:01:30.356 --> 00:01:33.189
till it springs back,
catapulting him pondward

00:01:33.259 --> 00:01:34.521
and splash.

00:01:34.594 --> 00:01:36.858
He'll sink like a log.

00:01:36.930 --> 00:01:38.864
But, Flotter... logs float.

00:01:38.932 --> 00:01:41.958
Details, details.

00:01:42.035 --> 00:01:43.593
That is a terrible plan.

00:01:43.670 --> 00:01:45.729
It's him!

00:01:45.805 --> 00:01:48.365
The name's Trevis,
and you are?

00:01:48.441 --> 00:01:51.638
Flotter. Flotter T. Water III.

00:01:51.711 --> 00:01:54.202
Well, of course you are, drippy.

00:01:54.280 --> 00:01:55.406
You.

00:01:55.482 --> 00:01:58.883
Naomi Wildman,
but my friends call me Naomi.

00:01:58.985 --> 00:02:01.476
I don't recognize your element.

00:02:01.554 --> 00:02:04.819
You're not earth or water
or plasma.

00:02:04.891 --> 00:02:06.051
I'm human.

00:02:06.126 --> 00:02:07.286
Where do you live?

00:02:07.360 --> 00:02:09.089
In space.

00:02:09.162 --> 00:02:10.789
Nobody lives in space.

00:02:10.864 --> 00:02:11.831
She does...

00:02:11.898 --> 00:02:14.196
on a starship called Voyager.

00:02:14.267 --> 00:02:15.598
I'm an explorer.

00:02:15.668 --> 00:02:16.828
Really?

00:02:16.903 --> 00:02:19.633
An explorer.

00:02:19.706 --> 00:02:20.832
Timber.

00:02:20.907 --> 00:02:22.169
What's that like?

00:02:22.242 --> 00:02:25.177
Well, you know...
space battles with aliens,

00:02:25.245 --> 00:02:26.507
strange anomalies.

00:02:26.579 --> 00:02:29.844
May I visit your starship?

00:02:29.916 --> 00:02:33.147
Well, I'll have to ask my mom.

00:02:33.219 --> 00:02:35.187
You know, for a monster,
you're very polite.

00:02:37.924 --> 00:02:41.189
That's because
I'm not a monster.

00:02:42.595 --> 00:02:43.857
You see that?

00:02:43.930 --> 00:02:45.522
I'm not scared one bit.

00:02:45.598 --> 00:02:48.863
My bark is worse than my bite.

00:02:48.935 --> 00:02:51.802
Maybe we jumped to conclusions
about him.

00:02:51.871 --> 00:02:53.862
Well, he may not be a monster,

00:02:54.007 --> 00:02:56.202
but he is stealing
my water with his roots.

00:02:56.276 --> 00:02:57.436
Stealing!

00:02:57.510 --> 00:03:02.140
Absurd!
Why, I ought to dry you out.

00:03:02.215 --> 00:03:04.183
And I ought to chop you down.

00:03:04.250 --> 00:03:05.945
You want a piece of me?

00:03:06.019 --> 00:03:08.817
Excuse me. It sounds like
you two need each other.

00:03:08.922 --> 00:03:11.288
I mean, think about it.

00:03:11.357 --> 00:03:12.949
Flotter, your water
helps his trees grow,

00:03:13.026 --> 00:03:16.154
and, Trevis, your branches
shade his pond from the sun.

00:03:16.229 --> 00:03:18.220
It's a well-known fact
that the sun

00:03:18.298 --> 00:03:19.560
makes water evaporate.

00:03:19.632 --> 00:03:20.656
She's got a point.

00:03:20.733 --> 00:03:22.633
The girl's a thinker.

00:03:22.702 --> 00:03:25.796
Now, shake hands and make up.

00:03:31.244 --> 00:03:33.178
Ugh... moist palms.

00:03:33.246 --> 00:03:35.510
Sappy fingers.

00:03:35.582 --> 00:03:37.174
Neelix to Holodeck 2.

00:03:37.250 --> 00:03:38.376
Naomi here.

00:03:38.451 --> 00:03:39.577
It's bedtime.

00:03:39.652 --> 00:03:41.415
Can't I stay a little longer?

00:03:41.487 --> 00:03:42.749
You know the rules.

00:03:42.822 --> 00:03:45.382
Besides, someone special
wants to say good night.

00:03:45.458 --> 00:03:46.857
Mom!

00:03:46.926 --> 00:03:49.053
Computer, end program.

00:03:49.128 --> 00:03:50.493
And how's Flotter?

00:03:50.563 --> 00:03:53.794
Grouchy as ever, but we made
a new friend today named Trevis.

00:03:53.866 --> 00:03:55.629
I'll introduce him
to you tomorrow

00:03:55.702 --> 00:03:56.999
as soon as you get home.

00:03:59.272 --> 00:04:00.603
I'm afraid the away mission

00:04:00.673 --> 00:04:02.504
may take a few more days,
sweetheart.

00:04:02.575 --> 00:04:03.667
Days?

00:04:03.743 --> 00:04:05.210
Yes...

00:04:05.278 --> 00:04:08.304
but I'm bringing you back some
beautiful sillinite crystals

00:04:08.381 --> 00:04:10.679
and lots of holopictures
for your data album.

00:04:10.750 --> 00:04:12.775
Now be a good girl
and get ready for bed

00:04:12.852 --> 00:04:14.479
while I talk to Neelix.

00:04:14.554 --> 00:04:15.816
All right.

00:04:15.888 --> 00:04:17.185
Sweet dreams.

00:04:23.229 --> 00:04:24.321
Samantha?

00:04:24.397 --> 00:04:26.422
We ran into an ion storm.

00:04:26.499 --> 00:04:28.126
How bad is it?

00:04:28.201 --> 00:04:29.532
We took a real beating.

00:04:29.602 --> 00:04:31.263
We're trying to make repairs,

00:04:31.337 --> 00:04:32.998
but there's
another storm on the way.

00:04:34.073 --> 00:04:35.005
Better go.

00:04:35.074 --> 00:04:36.769
Say good night for me?

00:04:38.878 --> 00:04:40.470
I've lost the com signal.

00:04:40.546 --> 00:04:43.481
A level-7 ionic front is
closing aft at 33,000 kph.

00:04:43.549 --> 00:04:45.517
I need more power
to the thrusters

00:04:45.585 --> 00:04:46.847
if I'm going to outrun it.

00:04:46.986 --> 00:04:48.419
I'll see what I can do.

00:04:48.488 --> 00:04:50.479
The leading edge is approaching.

00:04:50.556 --> 00:04:52.319
I've given all the power
I can spare, Tom.

00:04:52.392 --> 00:04:53.518
It's not enough.

00:04:53.593 --> 00:04:55.458
I can't keep ahead
of this thing.

00:04:55.528 --> 00:04:57.223
Brace for impact!

00:06:55.181 --> 00:06:56.978
Mayday, mayday.

00:06:57.049 --> 00:06:58.311
Delta Flyer to Voyager.

00:06:58.384 --> 00:07:00.477
We need assistance.

00:07:00.553 --> 00:07:03.784
Warp drive is...
Impulse power is down.

00:07:03.856 --> 00:07:06.689
...thrusters only.

00:07:06.759 --> 00:07:10.024
...ion storms damaged
our primary systems.

00:07:10.096 --> 00:07:12.564
Life support is failing.

00:07:12.632 --> 00:07:15.533
We're searching
for an emergency landing site.

00:07:15.601 --> 00:07:17.432
We require immediate...

00:07:20.940 --> 00:07:22.805
That was
their last transmission.

00:07:22.942 --> 00:07:24.705
We haven't been able
to raise them since.

00:07:24.777 --> 00:07:26.438
If they're looking
for a place to land,

00:07:26.512 --> 00:07:27.945
they must be
in pretty bad shape.

00:07:28.014 --> 00:07:29.345
Anything on long-range sensors?

00:07:29.415 --> 00:07:32.111
We lost their signature
when the second ion storm hit,

00:07:32.185 --> 00:07:34.153
but we've triangulated
the coordinates

00:07:34.220 --> 00:07:35.346
of the distress call.

00:07:35.421 --> 00:07:36.820
They've entered
a planetary system

00:07:36.923 --> 00:07:38.288
about.6 light-years from here.

00:07:38.357 --> 00:07:40.086
Problem is, there's
another ion storm...

00:07:40.159 --> 00:07:41.626
a level-5...
blocking our path.

00:07:41.694 --> 00:07:43.594
Level-5?

00:07:43.663 --> 00:07:45.324
We've been through worse.

00:07:45.398 --> 00:07:46.831
Let's just batten
down the hatches

00:07:46.933 --> 00:07:48.093
and reinforce the shields.

00:07:48.167 --> 00:07:49.191
We're not going to let

00:07:49.268 --> 00:07:51.133
a little bad weather
stand in our way.

00:07:51.204 --> 00:07:52.136
What about Naomi?

00:07:52.205 --> 00:07:54.105
I guess somebody's going to have

00:07:54.173 --> 00:07:56.403
to explain
why her mother's not back.

00:07:56.476 --> 00:07:58.842
Maybe we shouldn't
tell her anything.

00:07:58.978 --> 00:08:00.240
Why not?

00:08:00.313 --> 00:08:03.248
She's a very sensitive girl.

00:08:03.316 --> 00:08:05.409
I-I don't want to alarm
her unnecessarily.

00:08:05.485 --> 00:08:07.180
With any luck,
we'll have her mother back

00:08:07.253 --> 00:08:08.584
before she starts to worry.

00:08:08.654 --> 00:08:10.622
Well, you're closer to her
than anyone.

00:08:10.690 --> 00:08:12.783
I'm inclined to let you
take the lead on this.

00:08:12.925 --> 00:08:14.119
Thanks, Captain.

00:08:14.193 --> 00:08:16.661
All right.
Consider it your mission

00:08:16.729 --> 00:08:17.991
to keep her occupied.

00:08:18.064 --> 00:08:19.122
Aye, Captain.

00:08:19.198 --> 00:08:20.222
Dismissed.

00:08:25.304 --> 00:08:26.532
I was thinking...

00:08:26.606 --> 00:08:27.732
Oh?

00:08:27.807 --> 00:08:30.207
It's time I carried
my weight around here.

00:08:30.276 --> 00:08:34.212
Ah. They could use a hand
in the airponics bay.

00:08:34.280 --> 00:08:37.545
I was thinking
more of the Bridge.

00:08:37.617 --> 00:08:39.084
Captain's Assistant.

00:08:39.151 --> 00:08:40.675
Would I get to fly the ship?

00:08:40.753 --> 00:08:43.745
Well, we'd have to take
it up with the Captain.

00:08:46.459 --> 00:08:48.120
We need to check
the internal sensors.

00:08:48.194 --> 00:08:51.061
Neelix, don't move.

00:08:51.130 --> 00:08:52.688
What's wrong?

00:08:52.765 --> 00:08:54.528
The Borg lady.

00:08:56.302 --> 00:08:58.133
She has a name, you know.

00:08:58.204 --> 00:09:02.868
Seven of Nine, Tertiary Adjunct
of Unimatrix Zero One.

00:09:02.942 --> 00:09:04.773
Don't look.

00:09:04.877 --> 00:09:06.208
She'll assimilate you.

00:09:06.279 --> 00:09:08.304
Naomi, Seven is a nice person

00:09:08.381 --> 00:09:11.248
and she's a valuable member
of this crew.

00:09:11.317 --> 00:09:13.217
I don't want to be
in her collective.

00:09:13.286 --> 00:09:15.481
I don't think
there's much danger of that.

00:09:15.555 --> 00:09:16.453
Hey, Neelix.

00:09:16.522 --> 00:09:17.511
Hey, Naomi.

00:09:17.590 --> 00:09:19.182
Neelix, can I talk with you?

00:09:19.258 --> 00:09:20.782
Yeah. I'll be right back.

00:09:22.228 --> 00:09:24.492
Sick Bay's running short
on emergency medkits.

00:09:24.564 --> 00:09:25.690
We're going to need a few more

00:09:25.765 --> 00:09:27.596
if we send another away team
after the shuttle.

00:09:27.667 --> 00:09:30.500
I've got half a dozen
stockpiled in Cargo Bay 2.

00:09:30.570 --> 00:09:32.800
How is she?

00:09:32.872 --> 00:09:36.535
On the Naomi anxiety
scale of one to ten...

00:09:36.609 --> 00:09:39.976
where one is a touch of insomnia
and ten is a panic attack...

00:09:40.046 --> 00:09:41.240
about five.

00:09:42.348 --> 00:09:44.748
Is this chair occupied?

00:09:44.817 --> 00:09:48.116
Yes or no would suffice.

00:09:48.187 --> 00:09:49.552
No.

00:09:49.622 --> 00:09:51.180
I mean, yes.

00:09:51.257 --> 00:09:52.519
Explain.

00:09:52.592 --> 00:09:53.820
You can't sit here.

00:09:53.960 --> 00:09:56.121
Somebody else is sitting here.

00:09:56.195 --> 00:09:57.685
Very well.

00:10:01.200 --> 00:10:04.067
So... I thought we'd pay
another visit to Sick Bay.

00:10:04.136 --> 00:10:06.604
The Doctor says he has time
to give you a...

00:10:06.672 --> 00:10:08.105
botany lesson.

00:10:08.174 --> 00:10:09.471
What's wrong?

00:10:11.644 --> 00:10:13.839
I am Borg.

00:10:13.913 --> 00:10:15.505
No, you're not.

00:10:16.782 --> 00:10:18.579
Could we go
to the holodeck first?

00:10:18.651 --> 00:10:20.812
I want to play
another Flotter story.

00:10:20.886 --> 00:10:23.047
Well, the Doctor's
expecting you.

00:10:23.122 --> 00:10:25.056
I don't like Sick Bay.

00:10:25.124 --> 00:10:25.988
Why not?

00:10:26.058 --> 00:10:28.356
It's full of creepy things...

00:10:28.427 --> 00:10:30.725
alien organs and hyposprays.

00:10:30.796 --> 00:10:32.229
Well, that's not true.

00:10:32.298 --> 00:10:34.357
The Doctor talks too much.

00:10:34.433 --> 00:10:36.731
Well, that's his way.

00:10:36.802 --> 00:10:39.202
Can't you reprogram him
or something?

00:10:39.271 --> 00:10:42.172
Oh, I-I don't think
he'd like that very much.

00:10:43.275 --> 00:10:44.401
Come on.

00:10:49.482 --> 00:10:52.280
Rumor has it
there's a planetoid around here.

00:10:52.351 --> 00:10:53.545
Sorry, Tom.

00:10:53.619 --> 00:10:55.780
The storm
is throwing off my readings.

00:10:55.855 --> 00:10:57.880
There's definitely
a big rock nearby.

00:10:58.024 --> 00:10:59.252
I just can't find it.

00:10:59.325 --> 00:11:00.883
The wave front
is accelerating.

00:11:00.960 --> 00:11:02.222
How long till it hits us?

00:11:02.294 --> 00:11:03.591
Less than two minutes.

00:11:03.663 --> 00:11:06.188
Great. That gives me 30 seconds
to land this thing.

00:11:06.265 --> 00:11:08.028
Samantha,
I don't mean to rush you.

00:11:08.100 --> 00:11:09.192
Got it.

00:11:09.268 --> 00:11:10.428
Class-M atmosphere,

00:11:10.503 --> 00:11:12.733
nickel-iron core,
bemonite mantle.

00:11:12.805 --> 00:11:16.741
Bemonite? I want to land
this shuttle, not bury it.

00:11:16.809 --> 00:11:19.403
73,000 kilometers,
bearing 0 mark 4.

00:11:26.652 --> 00:11:28.916
We've entered
the upper atmosphere.

00:11:30.156 --> 00:11:32.556
Nothing but impact craters,
volcanoes...

00:11:32.625 --> 00:11:33.990
We can't land here.

00:11:34.060 --> 00:11:35.652
The storm is closing.

00:11:35.728 --> 00:11:38.060
Increasing shields to maximum.

00:11:38.130 --> 00:11:41.099
Just keep us away from the
volcanoes and we'll be okay.

00:11:41.167 --> 00:11:45.627
I've got a big meteor crater,
500 kilometers across, 3.7 deep.

00:11:45.705 --> 00:11:46.797
I'll take it.

00:11:46.872 --> 00:11:48.464
Starboard thrusters are down.

00:11:48.541 --> 00:11:51.772
Tuvok, if you don't have
something positive to say...

00:11:51.844 --> 00:11:53.004
We're coming in too fast.

00:11:53.079 --> 00:11:54.046
Hang on!

00:12:04.623 --> 00:12:07.592
The Flyer has landed.

00:12:13.632 --> 00:12:17.068
She needs
immediate medical assistance.

00:12:28.614 --> 00:12:30.582
What happened?

00:12:31.617 --> 00:12:33.084
We made it.

00:12:34.453 --> 00:12:36.580
Delta Flyer's first landing.

00:12:37.790 --> 00:12:39.223
Where...

00:12:39.291 --> 00:12:42.158
About three kilometers
beneath the surface.

00:12:42.228 --> 00:12:45.322
At least our primary
hull's still in one piece.

00:12:45.397 --> 00:12:46.830
Wish I felt the same.

00:12:46.899 --> 00:12:48.526
You'll be all right.

00:12:48.601 --> 00:12:51.502
Minor concussion,
a few fractures...

00:12:51.570 --> 00:12:53.504
nothing I can't handle.

00:12:53.572 --> 00:12:56.507
You're a great nurse,
but you're a lousy liar.

00:12:59.078 --> 00:13:02.775
You've got a punctured kidney
and you're bleeding internally.

00:13:02.848 --> 00:13:04.679
You need surgery.

00:13:04.750 --> 00:13:06.183
Voyager?

00:13:06.252 --> 00:13:09.346
I've transmitted
another distress call.

00:13:09.421 --> 00:13:10.683
No response.

00:13:10.756 --> 00:13:12.189
It's all this rock.

00:13:12.258 --> 00:13:14.692
I've got to talk to Naomi;
let her know we're okay.

00:13:15.928 --> 00:13:17.555
Conserve your strength, Ensign.

00:13:17.630 --> 00:13:20.292
Mr. Paris and I have
the situation under control.

00:13:20.366 --> 00:13:21.833
Nice bedside manner, Tuvok.

00:13:21.967 --> 00:13:24.527
Sam, I'm going to give
you a mild sedative

00:13:24.603 --> 00:13:26.230
and something for the pain.

00:13:33.612 --> 00:13:36.547
Any chance we could
abandon the shuttle,

00:13:36.615 --> 00:13:38.207
make our way on foot?

00:13:38.284 --> 00:13:39.512
Unlikely.

00:13:39.585 --> 00:13:42.110
Not only are we buried
under several kilotons of rock,

00:13:42.188 --> 00:13:43.780
but the atmosphere
in this cavern

00:13:43.856 --> 00:13:45.380
is flooded with fluorine gas.

00:13:47.126 --> 00:13:51.586
Nothing to do but sit back
and enjoy the view.

00:13:54.433 --> 00:13:56.264
Captain's Log, supplemental.

00:13:56.335 --> 00:13:57.597
We've weathered the ion storm

00:13:57.670 --> 00:14:00.468
and tracked the Delta Flyer
to an M-class planetoid.

00:14:01.774 --> 00:14:03.799
I'm picking up a residual
impulse signature

00:14:03.909 --> 00:14:05.171
in the upper atmosphere.

00:14:05.244 --> 00:14:07.178
Try to pinpoint their location.

00:14:07.246 --> 00:14:08.508
How's our littlest crew member?

00:14:08.581 --> 00:14:10.014
She misses her mother,

00:14:10.082 --> 00:14:11.982
but I don't think
she suspects anything.

00:14:12.051 --> 00:14:14.178
I was just about
to take her to the holodeck

00:14:14.253 --> 00:14:15.515
for some more storytelling.

00:14:15.588 --> 00:14:16.816
Call me an optimist, Neelix,

00:14:16.922 --> 00:14:18.822
but I'm still counting
on a happy ending.

00:14:18.891 --> 00:14:20.153
Me, too.

00:14:20.226 --> 00:14:22.251
Got it!
The impulse wake leads

00:14:22.328 --> 00:14:25.422
to the northern hemisphere:
Coordinates 121 mark 16.

00:14:25.497 --> 00:14:26.691
Any sign of them?

00:14:26.765 --> 00:14:29.928
Plasma fires...
hull fragments...

00:14:30.002 --> 00:14:32.129
Either they vaporized on impact

00:14:32.204 --> 00:14:33.671
or they're buried
beneath the surface.

00:14:33.739 --> 00:14:35.263
Any life signs?

00:14:35.341 --> 00:14:38.504
Maybe they beamed out
before the crash.

00:14:38.577 --> 00:14:41.512
Harry, anything?

00:14:41.580 --> 00:14:43.411
Nothing.

00:14:43.482 --> 00:14:47.077
We built the Delta Flyer
to take a lot of punishment.

00:14:47.152 --> 00:14:49.177
I'm betting it held together.

00:14:49.255 --> 00:14:52.986
Commander, take rescue teams
down to that crater.

00:14:53.058 --> 00:14:54.582
If sensors can't find them,

00:14:54.660 --> 00:14:56.252
we'll have to do it
the hard way.

00:14:56.328 --> 00:14:57.295
Harry.

00:15:00.766 --> 00:15:04.361
Now, see the organelle
just over there?

00:15:04.436 --> 00:15:07.667
The one that looks like
a little bitty potato?

00:15:07.740 --> 00:15:09.173
The mitochondria?

00:15:09.241 --> 00:15:10.333
Yes.

00:15:10.409 --> 00:15:12.434
"Mitochondria:
The warp core of the cell."

00:15:12.511 --> 00:15:13.603
Exactly.

00:15:13.679 --> 00:15:15.044
Now, what if I told you

00:15:15.114 --> 00:15:17.412
that this fellow
was invited to dinner,

00:15:17.483 --> 00:15:20.077
but never got around
to leaving?

00:15:20.152 --> 00:15:21.517
What do you mean?

00:15:21.587 --> 00:15:24.021
Well, turn back the clock
a few billion years

00:15:24.089 --> 00:15:26.489
to when cells first evolved.

00:15:26.558 --> 00:15:29.186
These early cells
had no mitochondria.

00:15:29.261 --> 00:15:31.821
They struggled along
without them, making do

00:15:31.964 --> 00:15:34.057
with whatever energy
sources they could find.

00:15:34.133 --> 00:15:36.294
Then, one day,

00:15:36.368 --> 00:15:38.734
a mitochondrial ancestor
arrived,

00:15:38.804 --> 00:15:42.001
broke though the cell wall
and made himself at home.

00:15:42.074 --> 00:15:43.735
They became friends?

00:15:43.809 --> 00:15:47.677
The correct term is "symbiosis."

00:15:47.746 --> 00:15:51.273
- Friends.
- Friends.

00:15:51.350 --> 00:15:55.116
My mom says cooperation is more
important than competition.

00:15:55.187 --> 00:15:57.087
Mm-hmm.

00:15:57.156 --> 00:16:00.353
She was supposed
to call me today.

00:16:00.426 --> 00:16:04.487
Well, she's probably
just a little busy.

00:16:04.563 --> 00:16:06.497
Now, let's have a look
at the cell wall.

00:16:06.565 --> 00:16:08.624
It looks simple enough,
but believe you me,

00:16:08.701 --> 00:16:10.498
there's more here
than meets the eye.

00:16:10.569 --> 00:16:11.695
Can we try to call her?

00:16:12.771 --> 00:16:13.703
Neelix.

00:16:13.772 --> 00:16:16.206
What a pleasure to see you.

00:16:16.275 --> 00:16:18.266
How was school today?

00:16:18.344 --> 00:16:19.811
Good.

00:16:19.912 --> 00:16:22.176
There's a time for school
and there's a time for...

00:16:22.247 --> 00:16:23.544
Flotter.

00:16:24.750 --> 00:16:26.684
Uh... aren't you
forgetting something?

00:16:26.752 --> 00:16:27.684
Oh.

00:16:27.753 --> 00:16:28.811
Thank you, Doctor.

00:16:28.887 --> 00:16:30.878
You're quite welcome,
Miss Wildman.

00:16:38.230 --> 00:16:41.461
In the blink of an eye,
there was Trevis above us.

00:16:41.533 --> 00:16:42.795
Then what happened?

00:16:42.868 --> 00:16:44.802
He turned out to be very nice.

00:16:44.870 --> 00:16:47.031
His bark was worse
than his bite.

00:16:48.307 --> 00:16:50.707
Where did you learn
to make such silly puns?

00:16:50.776 --> 00:16:52.038
You.

00:16:52.111 --> 00:16:53.305
Oh.

00:16:53.379 --> 00:16:55.847
Neelix, did you have
a favorite holodeck program

00:16:55.948 --> 00:16:57.210
when you were growing up?

00:16:57.282 --> 00:16:59.512
Well, we didn't have
any holodecks on Rinax,

00:16:59.585 --> 00:17:01.416
but it didn't matter
because we had

00:17:01.487 --> 00:17:03.648
a great big forest
right behind my house.

00:17:03.722 --> 00:17:04.654
Really?

00:17:04.723 --> 00:17:05.985
Uh-huh.

00:17:06.058 --> 00:17:09.550
And my sisters and I would
go exploring every day.

00:17:09.628 --> 00:17:11.653
We'd make up our own stories.

00:17:11.730 --> 00:17:13.459
Imagination.

00:17:13.532 --> 00:17:14.658
Exactly.

00:17:14.733 --> 00:17:17.429
Deck 6, Section 9.

00:17:17.503 --> 00:17:20.666
Where are your sisters now?

00:17:22.408 --> 00:17:25.969
Oh... they're
far away from here.

00:17:26.045 --> 00:17:28.104
I haven't seen them
in a very long time.

00:17:28.180 --> 00:17:30.045
How long?

00:17:30.115 --> 00:17:32.447
Many years.

00:17:32.518 --> 00:17:35.419
But you haven't been
on Voyager for that long.

00:17:35.487 --> 00:17:37.352
True, but before that,

00:17:37.423 --> 00:17:41.086
my work as a trader
kept me away from home.

00:17:41.160 --> 00:17:43.685
That's too bad.

00:17:47.332 --> 00:17:49.061
Do your sisters ever call you

00:17:49.134 --> 00:17:52.035
like my mom does when
she's on an away mission?

00:17:52.104 --> 00:17:53.036
No.

00:17:53.105 --> 00:17:55.437
I bet you miss them.

00:17:55.507 --> 00:17:57.407
I do, very much.

00:17:57.476 --> 00:17:58.944
Here we are.

00:18:01.880 --> 00:18:04.440
Computer, display
chapter headings

00:18:04.516 --> 00:18:06.643
The Adventures of Flotter.

00:18:06.718 --> 00:18:07.650
Let's see.

00:18:07.719 --> 00:18:10.153
"Flotter and the Tree Monster"?

00:18:10.222 --> 00:18:12.986
Played that one yesterday.

00:18:13.058 --> 00:18:15.458
Okay. "Trevis and the
Terribly Twisted Trunk."

00:18:15.527 --> 00:18:17.461
I promised I'd save
that one for mom.

00:18:17.529 --> 00:18:18.553
It's her favorite.

00:18:18.630 --> 00:18:22.794
"Flotter, Trevis
and the Ogre of Fire."

00:18:22.901 --> 00:18:24.664
Yeah. That one.

00:18:24.736 --> 00:18:27.000
Huh. That sounds a little scary.

00:18:27.072 --> 00:18:28.061
It's okay.

00:18:28.140 --> 00:18:30.040
I won't be scared
if you're with me.

00:18:33.245 --> 00:18:36.373
Once upon a time
in the Forest of Forever,

00:18:36.448 --> 00:18:38.643
Flotter and Trevis
encountered a strange element

00:18:38.717 --> 00:18:40.412
they'd never seen before.

00:18:46.091 --> 00:18:48.321
Trevis, you're on fire.

00:18:48.393 --> 00:18:49.917
I told him not to touch it,

00:18:49.995 --> 00:18:51.929
but this blockhead
never listens.

00:18:51.997 --> 00:18:53.965
Stop complaining and help him.

00:18:54.032 --> 00:18:55.260
Me?

00:18:55.334 --> 00:18:56.631
Water puts out fire.

00:19:00.038 --> 00:19:01.767
Oh, thank you.

00:19:01.874 --> 00:19:03.432
Hey, it worked.

00:19:03.509 --> 00:19:04.703
Watch this.

00:19:14.853 --> 00:19:17.344
Good thinking, Naomi.

00:19:17.422 --> 00:19:18.889
Who's the furball?

00:19:18.957 --> 00:19:20.720
The name's Neelix.

00:19:20.792 --> 00:19:22.885
What caused the fire?

00:19:22.961 --> 00:19:24.792
It came from up there.

00:19:24.863 --> 00:19:25.795
In a flash.

00:19:25.864 --> 00:19:27.798
Lightning.

00:19:27.900 --> 00:19:29.299
But the sky is clear.

00:19:29.368 --> 00:19:31.802
It doesn't look
like a thunderstorm.

00:19:31.904 --> 00:19:33.804
What's your theory, Naomi?

00:19:33.906 --> 00:19:36.670
There's only
one other explanation...

00:19:36.742 --> 00:19:39.472
the Ogre of Fire.

00:19:39.545 --> 00:19:41.445
The Ogre...

00:19:41.513 --> 00:19:43.413
...of Fire?

00:19:43.482 --> 00:19:45.177
Who's he?

00:19:45.250 --> 00:19:47.810
He is me!

00:19:47.886 --> 00:19:52.380
And I'm going to burn
this forest to the ground!

00:19:58.230 --> 00:20:01.461
Oh! Oh... Oh!

00:20:02.601 --> 00:20:04.228
Flotter!

00:20:14.146 --> 00:20:17.673
Maybe... we should
play another program.

00:20:17.749 --> 00:20:20.013
No, we have to find Flotter.

00:20:20.085 --> 00:20:21.848
Hello! Is anyone there?

00:20:21.987 --> 00:20:23.386
Over here.

00:20:24.523 --> 00:20:26.582
Trevis, are you all right?

00:20:26.658 --> 00:20:28.853
Uh-huh. A little hot
under the bark, maybe.

00:20:28.961 --> 00:20:30.758
What about Flotter?

00:20:32.364 --> 00:20:34.628
Is he dead?

00:20:36.268 --> 00:20:37.200
Neelix?

00:20:37.269 --> 00:20:38.293
Well, I...

00:20:38.370 --> 00:20:39.735
I don't know.

00:20:39.805 --> 00:20:41.238
He can't be dead.

00:20:41.306 --> 00:20:42.238
Flotter!

00:20:42.307 --> 00:20:43.399
I think it's your bedtime.

00:20:43.475 --> 00:20:45.238
But I want to find Flotter.

00:20:45.310 --> 00:20:47.870
Don't argue
with your godfather.

00:20:47.946 --> 00:20:49.038
Come on, now.

00:20:53.151 --> 00:20:54.379
Take this to Lieutenant Torres.

00:20:54.453 --> 00:20:56.045
You'll find the phaser drills
in Cargo Bay 3.

00:20:56.121 --> 00:20:57.179
Aye, sir.

00:20:57.256 --> 00:20:59.019
Are you sure you
have time for this?

00:20:59.091 --> 00:21:00.023
I know you're busy.

00:21:00.092 --> 00:21:01.184
No problem.

00:21:01.260 --> 00:21:02.989
Glad to be of service.

00:21:06.431 --> 00:21:07.921
Maybe a shade bluer.

00:21:08.000 --> 00:21:11.026
And the head's
a little disproportionate,

00:21:11.103 --> 00:21:12.365
don't you think?

00:21:12.437 --> 00:21:15.531
We're not shooting
for an exact replica, Neelix.

00:21:15.607 --> 00:21:16.835
Artistic license.

00:21:16.942 --> 00:21:18.034
Sorry.

00:21:18.110 --> 00:21:20.806
Guess I shouldn't barge
into your kitchen

00:21:20.879 --> 00:21:22.540
and tell you how to cook.

00:21:22.614 --> 00:21:25.674
Flotter... now there's a name
I haven't heard in a while.

00:21:25.751 --> 00:21:28.982
I used to be nuts about those
holostories when I was a kid.

00:21:29.054 --> 00:21:30.282
Did you see the one

00:21:30.355 --> 00:21:32.846
where Flotter suspects Trevis
to be a rubber tree?

00:21:32.958 --> 00:21:34.220
Not yet.

00:21:34.293 --> 00:21:37.023
He keeps trying to trip him
to see is if he'll bounce.

00:21:37.095 --> 00:21:38.858
Yeah, those two
were a lot of fun.

00:21:38.964 --> 00:21:40.363
Actually, the last scenario

00:21:40.432 --> 00:21:42.866
that Naomi chose was
pretty frightening.

00:21:42.934 --> 00:21:43.866
No fun at all.

00:21:43.935 --> 00:21:45.368
Kids love to be scared.

00:21:45.437 --> 00:21:46.836
Not Naomi.

00:21:46.905 --> 00:21:50.773
Computer, transfer the design
parameters to the replicator.

00:21:53.545 --> 00:21:54.978
How's she holding up?

00:21:55.047 --> 00:21:55.979
Fine.

00:21:56.048 --> 00:21:57.879
Right now, she's busy
with her homework.

00:21:58.016 --> 00:21:59.677
Neelix, what's wrong?

00:21:59.751 --> 00:22:02.185
Everything.
Everything's wrong!

00:22:02.254 --> 00:22:05.417
Lon storms, crash landings,
alien attacks...

00:22:05.490 --> 00:22:08.254
a starship's no place
for a child.

00:22:09.294 --> 00:22:10.488
I don't know.

00:22:10.562 --> 00:22:12.826
I'd say Naomi's pretty lucky
to be growing up on Voyager.

00:22:12.898 --> 00:22:13.956
Lucky?

00:22:14.032 --> 00:22:14.999
Think about it.

00:22:15.067 --> 00:22:17.763
Think about all the things
she's experienced...

00:22:17.836 --> 00:22:19.531
stars being born, supernovas,

00:22:19.604 --> 00:22:23.062
life-forms no one from the Alpha
Quadrant has seen before.

00:22:23.141 --> 00:22:25.837
When I was a kid,
I would have given anything

00:22:25.944 --> 00:22:27.673
for a chance like this.

00:22:27.746 --> 00:22:29.839
Well, here goes.

00:22:39.291 --> 00:22:40.815
Hi, Neelix.

00:22:40.892 --> 00:22:43.224
Did you miss me?

00:22:43.295 --> 00:22:46.059
You know, I forgot
how ugly this guy was.

00:22:46.131 --> 00:22:48.929
Thanks, Ensign.

00:22:58.910 --> 00:23:00.878
Naomi.

00:23:02.080 --> 00:23:04.207
Guess who I found
in the replicator.

00:23:04.282 --> 00:23:05.806
Thanks,

00:23:05.951 --> 00:23:09.512
but that's not really Flotter.

00:23:09.588 --> 00:23:12.955
Well, Flotter's
not really Flotter.

00:23:13.024 --> 00:23:16.016
He's just a holodeck character.

00:23:16.094 --> 00:23:18.528
What are you working on?

00:23:18.597 --> 00:23:20.827
I'm researching
the evaporation of water.

00:23:20.932 --> 00:23:22.832
Why?

00:23:22.934 --> 00:23:24.697
Well, I've been thinking.

00:23:24.770 --> 00:23:27.830
Water doesn't just
disappear when it's heated.

00:23:27.973 --> 00:23:29.838
It turns into invisible gas.

00:23:29.975 --> 00:23:33.433
So, if we could get the
forest to cool down enough,

00:23:33.512 --> 00:23:35.207
Flotter might reliquefy.

00:23:35.280 --> 00:23:36.907
Clever.

00:23:39.818 --> 00:23:42.048
I miss Mom.

00:23:42.120 --> 00:23:43.849
I know you do.

00:23:43.955 --> 00:23:46.219
When's she coming back?

00:23:48.727 --> 00:23:50.092
Soon.

00:23:50.162 --> 00:23:52.357
Why hasn't she called?

00:23:52.431 --> 00:23:54.729
She must be very busy

00:23:54.800 --> 00:23:57.792
cataloguing all the geological
specimens she's collected.

00:23:57.869 --> 00:24:00.463
Has anybody talked to her?

00:24:02.340 --> 00:24:06.299
Well... not in a day
or two, but...

00:24:06.378 --> 00:24:08.812
"Starfleet Regulation 476-9:

00:24:08.914 --> 00:24:11.678
"All away teams must
report to the Bridge

00:24:11.750 --> 00:24:14.310
at least once every 24 hours."

00:24:14.386 --> 00:24:16.980
You really are going to make an
excellent Captain's Assistant.

00:24:17.055 --> 00:24:19.421
What if something bad
happened to them?

00:24:19.491 --> 00:24:22.619
I'm sure everything's fine.

00:24:22.694 --> 00:24:24.685
Come on now, bed.

00:24:24.763 --> 00:24:27.357
Promise to wake me up
if Mommy calls?

00:24:27.432 --> 00:24:28.524
Promise.

00:24:28.600 --> 00:24:30.534
Even if it's 0200 hours?

00:24:30.602 --> 00:24:33.366
Even if it's 0200 hours.

00:24:33.438 --> 00:24:35.906
Sweet dreams.

00:24:38.944 --> 00:24:41.037
Neelix?

00:25:10.909 --> 00:25:15.107
Computer, access
Personal Database Neelix.

00:25:15.180 --> 00:25:16.704
File index 291.

00:25:18.416 --> 00:25:19.815
Hello, Alixia.

00:25:19.951 --> 00:25:23.910
I'm sorry it's been
so many weeks

00:25:23.989 --> 00:25:25.456
since I've thought about you,

00:25:25.524 --> 00:25:27.617
but we've been very busy
here on Voyager.

00:25:27.692 --> 00:25:30.593
I miss you.

00:25:30.662 --> 00:25:35.463
My goddaughter, Naomi,
she's in trouble.

00:25:35.534 --> 00:25:37.729
We're in trouble.

00:25:39.104 --> 00:25:42.267
She may lose her mother.

00:25:42.340 --> 00:25:46.367
Alixia, you always knew
the right thing to do,

00:25:46.444 --> 00:25:48.275
the right thing to say.

00:25:51.316 --> 00:25:52.749
I wish you were here to help me.

00:26:05.730 --> 00:26:07.197
Come on!

00:26:07.265 --> 00:26:08.698
Hurry!

00:26:13.138 --> 00:26:14.537
We're under attack!

00:26:18.410 --> 00:26:20.173
Get up!

00:26:24.215 --> 00:26:26.809
The metreon cascade!
Run!

00:26:58.383 --> 00:27:00.010
Computer, switch
to polythermal imaging

00:27:00.085 --> 00:27:01.985
and enhance resolution.

00:27:02.053 --> 00:27:04.715
Neelix, do you require
assistance?

00:27:04.789 --> 00:27:07.519
No, no, I was just passing by.

00:27:07.592 --> 00:27:10.891
I thought I'd pay you a visit,
see how things were going.

00:27:10.962 --> 00:27:12.953
How are things going?

00:27:13.031 --> 00:27:15.124
I'm mapping the caverns
surrounding the crash site.

00:27:15.200 --> 00:27:17.134
How far do they extend?

00:27:17.202 --> 00:27:19.602
Approximately 37 kilometers.

00:27:19.671 --> 00:27:22.504
What about the search...
anything new?

00:27:22.574 --> 00:27:24.474
Every scan reveals
something new,

00:27:24.542 --> 00:27:26.442
but as yet, little of relevance.

00:27:28.313 --> 00:27:30.304
Seven...

00:27:30.382 --> 00:27:33.977
your family...
your human family...

00:27:34.052 --> 00:27:36.316
do you ever think about them?

00:27:36.388 --> 00:27:38.549
Infrequently.

00:27:38.623 --> 00:27:41.319
I was only six years old
when I was assimilated.

00:27:41.393 --> 00:27:44.362
Not much older
than Naomi is now.

00:27:44.429 --> 00:27:46.693
Do you miss your parents?

00:27:46.765 --> 00:27:49.063
I barely remember them.

00:27:49.134 --> 00:27:51.534
Maybe that's a blessing.

00:27:53.571 --> 00:27:55.038
Rescue team alpha
to Seven of Nine.

00:27:55.106 --> 00:27:56.232
Yes, Commander.

00:27:56.307 --> 00:27:57.934
We need that data.

00:27:58.009 --> 00:28:01.172
I will meet you
at the transporter site.

00:28:03.248 --> 00:28:05.273
I adapted.

00:28:05.350 --> 00:28:08.217
The child Naomi
will adapt as well.

00:28:08.286 --> 00:28:10.345
Borg wisdom.

00:28:15.694 --> 00:28:18.458
Lieutenant, get me
an update from beta team.

00:28:18.530 --> 00:28:21.055
They haven't checked in
for over an hour.

00:28:21.132 --> 00:28:22.156
Coffee, anyone?

00:28:22.233 --> 00:28:23.666
Captain?

00:28:23.735 --> 00:28:25.134
No, thanks. I've had enough.

00:28:25.203 --> 00:28:27.000
One more cup
and I'll jump to warp.

00:28:27.072 --> 00:28:28.004
Any news?

00:28:28.073 --> 00:28:29.700
I'm afraid not.

00:28:29.774 --> 00:28:32.334
No debris, no life signs?

00:28:32.410 --> 00:28:34.503
We've got three teams
beneath the surface

00:28:34.579 --> 00:28:35.603
and so far, nothing.

00:28:35.680 --> 00:28:38.376
Well, so much
for that happy ending.

00:28:38.450 --> 00:28:41.351
We'll turn that planetoid
inside out if we have to,

00:28:41.419 --> 00:28:44.650
but I think we have to be
prepared for the worst.

00:28:44.723 --> 00:28:47.021
Maybe it's time you told Naomi.

00:28:47.092 --> 00:28:49.083
No, not yet.

00:28:49.160 --> 00:28:50.422
She's an astute girl.

00:28:50.495 --> 00:28:52.622
She must be aware that
something's wrong by now.

00:28:52.697 --> 00:28:54.665
She's been asking
a lot of tough questions.

00:28:54.733 --> 00:28:56.724
"Why hasn't her mother
filed a status report?"

00:28:56.801 --> 00:28:57.995
"What if she's in trouble?"

00:28:58.069 --> 00:29:00.230
But I've got a big day
planned for her tomorrow.

00:29:00.305 --> 00:29:01.397
Plenty of distractions.

00:29:01.473 --> 00:29:03.634
She won't have time
to be worried.

00:29:03.708 --> 00:29:05.733
Your mission was
to keep her occupied,

00:29:05.810 --> 00:29:06.777
not to lie to her.

00:29:06.845 --> 00:29:08.244
First thing in the morning,

00:29:08.313 --> 00:29:10.281
I want you to explain
the situation.

00:29:10.348 --> 00:29:12.782
I don't think
that's such a good idea.

00:29:12.884 --> 00:29:14.579
Why not?

00:29:14.652 --> 00:29:17.314
Like I told you,
she's sensitive.

00:29:17.388 --> 00:29:19.618
All the more reason
to answer her questions.

00:29:19.691 --> 00:29:23.320
With all due respect, Captain,
I'm her godfather.

00:29:23.394 --> 00:29:25.624
I know what's best for her.

00:29:27.165 --> 00:29:29.292
Neelix...

00:29:39.344 --> 00:29:41.005
I realize you care about Naomi

00:29:41.079 --> 00:29:43.274
and you are only
trying to protect her,

00:29:43.348 --> 00:29:45.441
but you've got
to tell her the truth.

00:29:47.485 --> 00:29:48.747
"Good morning, Naomi.

00:29:48.820 --> 00:29:50.720
"Would you like some papalla
juice with your cereal?

00:29:50.789 --> 00:29:51.813
"And, oh, by the way,

00:29:51.890 --> 00:29:53.585
your mother is buried
under 30 kilotons of rock."

00:29:53.658 --> 00:29:54.750
Neelix...

00:29:54.826 --> 00:29:56.350
When we know something
for sure...

00:29:56.427 --> 00:30:01.160
when we find her mother,
alive or dead...

00:30:01.232 --> 00:30:04.827
I'll tell her then.

00:30:04.903 --> 00:30:06.268
Not before.

00:30:06.337 --> 00:30:08.828
If you can't do it, I will.

00:30:08.907 --> 00:30:10.670
You don't have the right!

00:30:10.742 --> 00:30:13.734
You don't understand
what's at stake here!

00:30:13.812 --> 00:30:14.744
When you were her age,

00:30:14.813 --> 00:30:16.280
you were safe
and sound on Earth

00:30:16.347 --> 00:30:18.542
with two healthy parents
to take care of you.

00:30:18.616 --> 00:30:19.810
You never had to worry

00:30:19.884 --> 00:30:21.852
about the possibility
of being alone!

00:30:21.953 --> 00:30:24.717
You take it from me...
you wouldn't have liked it.

00:30:26.257 --> 00:30:27.189
Oh, I know.

00:30:27.258 --> 00:30:30.955
You must identify
with Naomi's situation.

00:30:33.565 --> 00:30:38.502
When my family was killed,
I lost everything.

00:30:38.570 --> 00:30:40.800
I still have nightmares.

00:30:40.872 --> 00:30:43.864
It hasn't been easy.

00:30:43.942 --> 00:30:46.376
I don't want Naomi
to go through what I did.

00:30:46.444 --> 00:30:49.641
I understand and you're right,

00:30:49.714 --> 00:30:53.878
but this situation is different.

00:30:53.952 --> 00:30:55.283
How so?

00:30:59.224 --> 00:31:01.021
Naomi has you.

00:31:01.092 --> 00:31:04.323
Neelix, she has to be told,

00:31:04.395 --> 00:31:06.556
but I know she'll be better off

00:31:06.631 --> 00:31:09.464
having you here
to help her through it.

00:31:12.770 --> 00:31:15.068
First thing in the morning.

00:31:15.139 --> 00:31:17.630
We've got a few hours
until then.

00:31:17.709 --> 00:31:20.678
Why don't you come
back on the Bridge?

00:31:20.745 --> 00:31:21.973
Give us a hand?

00:31:25.516 --> 00:31:26.983
Ready, Tuvok?

00:31:27.051 --> 00:31:28.848
Ready.

00:31:35.126 --> 00:31:36.684
Cross your fingers.

00:31:40.431 --> 00:31:43.195
The magnetic relays
have overloaded.

00:31:43.268 --> 00:31:45.759
We better find another way
to polarize this hull

00:31:45.837 --> 00:31:48.203
or their sensors
won't be able to pick us up.

00:31:48.273 --> 00:31:49.740
We're never getting out of here.

00:31:49.807 --> 00:31:52.469
Do not give up hope.

00:31:52.543 --> 00:31:54.738
The probability
of our being rescued is low,

00:31:54.812 --> 00:31:56.473
but not statistically
impossible.

00:31:56.547 --> 00:31:58.515
Comforting.

00:31:58.583 --> 00:32:00.710
Who's going to look after Naomi?

00:32:00.785 --> 00:32:03.151
You should not concern yourself
with that now.

00:32:03.221 --> 00:32:05.212
How can you say that?

00:32:05.290 --> 00:32:06.450
My youngest child

00:32:06.524 --> 00:32:09.459
has been without a father
for four years,

00:32:09.527 --> 00:32:11.825
yet I am certain
of her well-being,

00:32:11.963 --> 00:32:16.297
that I conveyed my values
to her before leaving,

00:32:16.367 --> 00:32:18.062
and I have confidence
in the integrity

00:32:18.136 --> 00:32:19.660
of those around her.

00:32:19.737 --> 00:32:23.229
You have been an exemplary
mother to Naomi

00:32:23.308 --> 00:32:27.472
and she is in the hands
of people you trust.

00:32:27.545 --> 00:32:33.780
She will survive and prosper,
no matter what becomes of us.

00:32:36.054 --> 00:32:38.284
Thanks, Tuvok.

00:32:46.230 --> 00:32:47.925
Mom!

00:32:50.635 --> 00:32:52.330
Neelix?

00:33:06.951 --> 00:33:09.181
Computer, locate Neelix.

00:33:09.253 --> 00:33:11.187
Neelix is on the Bridge.

00:33:11.255 --> 00:33:12.449
Thanks.

00:33:28.706 --> 00:33:31.641
Strickler, we need
three more phaser drills.

00:33:31.709 --> 00:33:34.007
You two, pattern enhancers
and medkits.

00:33:34.078 --> 00:33:35.443
Aye, sir.

00:33:35.513 --> 00:33:39.609
We're going to have
to recalibrate these tricorders.

00:33:41.886 --> 00:33:43.513
Put us with the alpha team.

00:33:43.588 --> 00:33:44.850
Setting coordinates.

00:33:44.956 --> 00:33:46.651
Energize.

00:33:59.470 --> 00:34:01.301
Deck 1, Bridge.

00:34:07.345 --> 00:34:08.778
Chakotay to Voyager.

00:34:08.846 --> 00:34:12.179
We found what looks like a piece
of the starboard nacelle.

00:34:12.250 --> 00:34:13.979
Any sign of the shuttle itself?

00:34:14.052 --> 00:34:15.178
Not yet.

00:34:15.253 --> 00:34:17.187
Captain, the cavern has
collapsed ahead of us.

00:34:17.255 --> 00:34:19.587
However, I am reading a hull
signature behind the debris.

00:34:19.657 --> 00:34:21.249
The Flyer?

00:34:21.325 --> 00:34:22.917
I'll need to take
a closer reading.

00:34:22.994 --> 00:34:25.360
Do it. I want alpha and beta
teams to search for survivors.

00:34:25.430 --> 00:34:27.921
Tell Sick Bay to stand by
for heavy casualties.

00:34:30.468 --> 00:34:31.230
Naomi?

00:34:33.805 --> 00:34:35.033
Naomi...

00:34:44.916 --> 00:34:46.315
Naomi?

00:34:50.221 --> 00:34:52.121
Computer, locate Naomi Wildman.

00:34:52.190 --> 00:34:54.784
Naomi Wildman
is in her quarters.

00:35:13.544 --> 00:35:14.875
Clever.

00:35:18.282 --> 00:35:19.943
Computer, resume program

00:35:20.017 --> 00:35:22.747
"Flotter, Trevis
and the Ogre of Fire."

00:35:22.820 --> 00:35:24.117
Program activated.

00:35:25.890 --> 00:35:28.222
Commander, I'm reading
duranium alloys.

00:35:28.292 --> 00:35:29.919
I believe it is the shuttle.

00:35:29.994 --> 00:35:32.690
Approximately 80 meters
beneath this rubble.

00:35:32.763 --> 00:35:33.957
Life signs?

00:35:34.031 --> 00:35:35.623
None.

00:35:35.700 --> 00:35:37.668
Commander, without
life signs to lock on to,

00:35:37.735 --> 00:35:39.362
we cannot beam the crew out.

00:35:39.437 --> 00:35:41.132
Maybe we can transport
the entire ship

00:35:41.205 --> 00:35:42.137
to the shuttle bay.

00:35:42.206 --> 00:35:44.697
Through 50 kilotons of bemonite?

00:35:46.978 --> 00:35:48.275
Chakotay to Voyager.

00:35:48.346 --> 00:35:49.711
Janeway here.

00:35:49.780 --> 00:35:51.304
We think
we've found the shuttle,

00:35:51.382 --> 00:35:52.576
but we need to dig it out.

00:35:52.650 --> 00:35:55.175
Have all teams rendezvous
at my coordinates.

00:35:55.253 --> 00:35:56.242
Acknowledged.

00:35:56.320 --> 00:35:59.778
Phaser drills here and here.

00:35:59.857 --> 00:36:03.793
But, hey, B'Elanna,
look on the bright side.

00:36:03.928 --> 00:36:06.089
No more day-old pizza
laying around.

00:36:08.566 --> 00:36:11.797
And you'll never have
to watch another chapter

00:36:11.903 --> 00:36:13.632
of Captain Proton again.

00:36:13.704 --> 00:36:16.935
Warning. Life support
has fallen to critical levels.

00:36:17.008 --> 00:36:18.805
Don't mind the computer.

00:36:18.876 --> 00:36:21.538
She's just jealous
that I'm spending

00:36:21.612 --> 00:36:24.274
my last few minutes
talking to you.

00:36:28.753 --> 00:36:30.186
So long.

00:36:35.259 --> 00:36:36.521
Sam...

00:36:38.563 --> 00:36:40.554
it's your turn.

00:36:40.631 --> 00:36:45.125
I... haven't thought
what to say yet.

00:36:45.203 --> 00:36:48.001
Tuvok, why don't you go next?

00:36:49.040 --> 00:36:52.407
I prefer to make my farewells
in written form.

00:37:06.657 --> 00:37:08.682
Computer, begin recording.

00:37:08.759 --> 00:37:12.251
Encode message
for delivery to Naomi Wildman.

00:37:12.330 --> 00:37:14.958
Acknowledged.

00:37:15.032 --> 00:37:16.522
Hi, honey.

00:37:16.601 --> 00:37:19.570
I know you're feeling sad
right now,

00:37:19.637 --> 00:37:24.233
but I want you to listen
to me very carefully, okay?

00:37:27.178 --> 00:37:30.739
First of all, I love you.

00:37:32.516 --> 00:37:37.977
Second, I want you to know
that I'm proud of you,

00:37:38.055 --> 00:37:41.456
how smart you are, how funny,

00:37:41.525 --> 00:37:43.823
how kind you are
to other people.

00:37:43.961 --> 00:37:46.327
And I know that you are going
to grow up

00:37:46.397 --> 00:37:48.092
to do extraordinary things.

00:37:51.235 --> 00:37:56.605
Last... and I know
this is a hard one...

00:37:56.674 --> 00:37:58.835
try not to be scared.

00:37:58.976 --> 00:38:02.912
Warning. Oxygen depletion
in ten minutes.

00:38:02.980 --> 00:38:04.607
Listen to Neelix.

00:38:04.682 --> 00:38:07.776
He'll be taking care of you now.

00:38:10.755 --> 00:38:12.723
Bye, honey.

00:38:23.234 --> 00:38:24.667
Naomi?

00:38:24.735 --> 00:38:26.726
Go away!

00:38:26.804 --> 00:38:28.101
Where is she?

00:38:28.172 --> 00:38:31.141
She doesn't want to talk to you.

00:38:31.208 --> 00:38:32.334
You lied.

00:38:32.410 --> 00:38:34.401
I thought you vaporized.

00:38:34.478 --> 00:38:37.538
Naomi reliquefied me.

00:38:37.615 --> 00:38:39.014
Now leave.

00:38:39.083 --> 00:38:40.380
Computer, delete characters.

00:38:40.451 --> 00:38:42.009
Unable to comply.

00:38:42.086 --> 00:38:44.782
Holodeck controls
have been encoded.

00:38:45.990 --> 00:38:48.015
Delete us?

00:38:48.092 --> 00:38:50.026
I wonder if this liar can swim?

00:38:50.094 --> 00:38:53.825
We could always hang him
from one of my branches.

00:38:53.931 --> 00:38:55.159
Naomi.

00:38:56.901 --> 00:38:58.596
Please let me talk to you.

00:38:58.669 --> 00:39:00.933
It's okay.

00:39:01.005 --> 00:39:02.996
You be nice.

00:39:03.074 --> 00:39:05.008
No more lying.

00:39:19.623 --> 00:39:20.988
Hey, there.

00:39:21.058 --> 00:39:23.424
Is my mother dead?

00:39:24.829 --> 00:39:27.093
We don't know.

00:39:27.164 --> 00:39:29.098
What happened?

00:39:29.166 --> 00:39:32.397
The away team was trying
to avoid an ion storm.

00:39:32.470 --> 00:39:34.438
They had to land on a planet.

00:39:34.505 --> 00:39:36.166
I saw that crater.

00:39:36.240 --> 00:39:38.231
Something was burning.

00:39:38.309 --> 00:39:42.245
Plasma fires,
pieces of debris...

00:39:42.313 --> 00:39:44.281
but not the hull.

00:39:46.884 --> 00:39:49.546
Until we know
for sure what's happened,

00:39:49.620 --> 00:39:52.282
no one's giving up
on the rescue attempt.

00:39:52.356 --> 00:39:54.756
You really think
they might find her?

00:39:56.660 --> 00:39:59.561
Yes.

00:39:59.630 --> 00:40:00.722
How do I know

00:40:00.798 --> 00:40:02.857
you're telling me
the truth this time?

00:40:08.205 --> 00:40:10.230
I...

00:40:10.307 --> 00:40:13.367
I never told you this before...

00:40:13.444 --> 00:40:16.845
but when I was much younger,

00:40:16.914 --> 00:40:20.509
I lost my mom
in a terrible war...

00:40:20.584 --> 00:40:23.348
my father
and my sisters, too.

00:40:25.156 --> 00:40:29.752
It was the worst thing
that ever happened to me.

00:40:29.827 --> 00:40:31.761
Always wondering...

00:40:31.829 --> 00:40:33.296
How did they die?

00:40:33.364 --> 00:40:35.730
Were they worried about me?

00:40:35.800 --> 00:40:38.860
Could they still be alive?

00:40:39.003 --> 00:40:42.598
I thought if I could just
keep you from wondering...

00:40:42.673 --> 00:40:45.198
you wouldn't have to feel
what I did.

00:40:45.276 --> 00:40:48.439
You were pretending
that nothing was wrong...

00:40:48.512 --> 00:40:50.377
that nothing bad happened.

00:40:50.448 --> 00:40:52.313
Do you ever pretend

00:40:52.383 --> 00:40:54.715
that nothing bad happened
to your family?

00:40:56.554 --> 00:40:57.987
Sometimes.

00:40:58.055 --> 00:40:59.454
Does it help?

00:41:00.524 --> 00:41:01.786
Not really.

00:41:03.060 --> 00:41:05.460
Don't be sad, Neelix.

00:41:08.399 --> 00:41:09.957
All hands to emergency stations.

00:41:10.034 --> 00:41:12.400
We've got a level-8
ion storm approaching.

00:41:12.470 --> 00:41:13.835
Ion storm? What's that?

00:41:13.904 --> 00:41:14.836
The Ogre of Fire.

00:41:14.939 --> 00:41:16.338
He's attacking us again.

00:41:16.407 --> 00:41:18.466
We'd better get back
to your quarters.

00:41:18.542 --> 00:41:19.474
Naomi.

00:41:19.543 --> 00:41:21.010
Don't leave us.

00:41:21.078 --> 00:41:22.841
I'll be back.
I promise.

00:41:27.218 --> 00:41:27.318
Voyager to Chakotay.

00:41:27.318 --> 00:41:28.307
Voyager to Chakotay.

00:41:28.385 --> 00:41:29.443
Go ahead.

00:41:29.520 --> 00:41:31.283
We've got another
ion storm approaching.

00:41:31.355 --> 00:41:32.583
When it hits the planetoid,

00:41:32.656 --> 00:41:34.749
your entire cavern
is going to destabilize.

00:41:34.825 --> 00:41:35.849
Just a few more meters

00:41:35.993 --> 00:41:38.518
and we'll be close enough
to beam out the shuttle.

00:41:38.596 --> 00:41:40.063
How long before the storm hits?

00:41:40.130 --> 00:41:41.324
Six minutes.

00:41:41.398 --> 00:41:44.595
Make the most of it,
because it's all you've got.

00:41:52.276 --> 00:41:54.039
The storm is moving in.

00:41:54.111 --> 00:41:56.204
Shields down to 86 percent.

00:41:56.280 --> 00:41:58.271
Keep a transporter lock
on the away team.

00:41:58.349 --> 00:41:59.873
We'll give them
till the last second.

00:42:00.017 --> 00:42:02.679
Helm, lay in a course
out of here.

00:42:02.753 --> 00:42:04.277
Stand by to engage at warp 2.

00:42:04.355 --> 00:42:05.447
Aye, sir.

00:42:05.523 --> 00:42:09.220
Warning. Oxygen depletion
in two minutes.

00:42:09.293 --> 00:42:12.729
I never thought it would
come down to this...

00:42:12.796 --> 00:42:15.560
suffocating beneath
kilotons of rock

00:42:15.633 --> 00:42:17.692
on some nameless planetoid.

00:42:17.768 --> 00:42:21.499
Did you envision
a more heroic death?

00:42:21.572 --> 00:42:24.439
I didn't envision dying at all.

00:42:24.508 --> 00:42:28.774
In accepting the inevitable,
one finds peace.

00:42:30.381 --> 00:42:33.350
If that's another
Vulcan saying, Tuvok,

00:42:33.417 --> 00:42:35.977
I'll stick with
"live long and prosper."

00:42:40.724 --> 00:42:45.024
We're here.
We're here!

00:42:45.095 --> 00:42:46.187
Chakotay to Voyager.

00:42:46.263 --> 00:42:47.195
Yes, Commander.

00:42:47.264 --> 00:42:49.129
Pattern enhancers are in place.

00:42:49.199 --> 00:42:51.258
We're ready to transport
the Flyer.

00:42:51.335 --> 00:42:52.461
Locking on.

00:42:56.607 --> 00:42:59.371
They're in the shuttle bay.

00:42:59.443 --> 00:43:00.876
Helm, engage.

00:43:22.366 --> 00:43:23.833
Thank you.

00:43:29.974 --> 00:43:31.839
Captain's Log, supplemental.

00:43:31.909 --> 00:43:35.003
Ensign Wildman has recovered
from her injuries

00:43:35.079 --> 00:43:38.378
and the Delta Flyer,
though battered, is intact.

00:43:38.449 --> 00:43:40.474
And how are you today,
Mr. Trevis?

00:43:40.551 --> 00:43:43.645
Feeling a little stiff,
my slippery friend. And you?

00:43:43.721 --> 00:43:46.451
Well, now that you mention it,
I'm feeling a little washed out.

00:43:48.359 --> 00:43:50.190
Well, it's about time
you showed up.

00:43:50.260 --> 00:43:52.125
The tea is getting cold.

00:43:52.196 --> 00:43:54.061
Samantha?

00:43:54.131 --> 00:43:55.689
Is it really you?

00:43:55.766 --> 00:43:57.358
Long time no see.

00:43:57.434 --> 00:43:58.628
You're all grown up.

00:43:58.702 --> 00:43:59.862
I'm an Ensign now.

00:43:59.970 --> 00:44:01.437
I missed you.

00:44:01.505 --> 00:44:02.904
Likewise.

00:44:02.973 --> 00:44:04.770
Well, now that everyone's
reacquainted,

00:44:04.842 --> 00:44:06.810
I bet you're all eager
for a new adventure.

00:44:06.944 --> 00:44:08.377
Now that you mention it,

00:44:08.445 --> 00:44:10.811
there is a castle that I've
been meaning to explore.

00:44:10.948 --> 00:44:11.915
Castle?

00:44:11.982 --> 00:44:13.813
I hear a giant beetle
lives there.

00:44:13.951 --> 00:44:15.543
Come on, Neelix.

00:44:15.619 --> 00:44:16.745
You go ahead.

00:44:16.820 --> 00:44:17.787
See you later.

00:44:20.691 --> 00:44:22.591
Here's to happy endings.

00:44:22.660 --> 00:44:24.594
Captain!

00:44:24.662 --> 00:44:27.130
Just checking on my future
Captain's Assistant.

00:44:27.197 --> 00:44:30.598
Well, right now, she's off
to conquer a giant beetle.

00:44:30.668 --> 00:44:34.297
Oh, sounds
like a dangerous mission.

00:44:34.371 --> 00:44:36.032
She can handle it.

00:44:36.106 --> 00:44:37.630
She's a courageous girl.

00:44:37.708 --> 00:44:39.175
Oh...

00:44:39.243 --> 00:44:41.143
Did I ever tell you
about the time

00:44:41.211 --> 00:44:42.838
I flooded this entire forest?

00:44:42.946 --> 00:44:44.072
I was six years old.

00:44:44.148 --> 00:44:46.616
Flotter claimed we were
in for a dry spell,

00:44:46.684 --> 00:44:48.845
so I came up
with the obvious solution.

00:44:48.986 --> 00:44:50.715
Why not just divert the river?

00:44:50.788 --> 00:44:54.155
This entire forest was a swamp
by the time we were done.

00:44:54.224 --> 00:44:55.851
At which point, Stinger...

00:44:55.959 --> 00:44:56.857
Stinger?

00:44:56.994 --> 00:44:58.256
The biggest mosquito...
